---
import CaseStudy from '../../layouts/CaseStudy.astro';
---

<CaseStudy
  number="01"
  title="Building ePMS & HRMS automation from zero"
  subtitle="Two ERP modules tested by hand became a 20-minute automated suite, plus data-prep scripts that turned an hour of HRMS setup into minutes."
  description="Case study: a Python + Playwright + pytest framework for BRAC's ePMS and HRMS modules that cut regression from 2 hours to 20 minutes, and data-prep scripts that cut HRMS test-data setup from 1 hour to 10–12 minutes."
  facts={[
    { label: 'Role', value: 'Senior SQA Engineer · ePMS module owner · framework owner' },
    { label: 'Timeline', value: 'Apr – Oct 2026 · v1 in one month' },
    { label: 'Stack', value: 'Python · Playwright · pytest · Allure · GitLab' },
    { label: 'Scope', value: 'ePMS: Objective Setting → 360° feedback · HRMS: 5 core features · 2 data-prep flows' },
  ]}
  approach={[
    { lead: 'Designed the framework from scratch', text: "in Python with Playwright and pytest, structured around one employee's journey rather than around pages. The first version ran within a month; I kept refining it after." },
    { lead: 'Made environment a configuration choice,', text: 'so the same suite runs on dev, staging and a dedicated test environment.' },
    { lead: 'Handled variable form data dynamically', text: 'instead of hard-coding it, which removed the main source of false failures.' },
    { lead: 'Added Allure reporting and versioned everything in GitLab,', text: "so results are readable by people who don't write tests." },
    { lead: 'Built two scenario-based data-prep scripts', text: 'for Job Separation and Employee Transfer, kept separate from regression and smoke runs, to create ready-to-use data on demand.' },
  ]}
  results={[
    "One employee's full ePMS journey automated end to end, from Objective Setting to the 360° feedback review.",
    'HRMS basic flow automated for the smoke suite, covering five core features: employee creation, transfer, job separation, higher study and travel.',
    'Regression cut from about <strong>2 hours</strong> by hand to <strong>20 minutes</strong>, on dev, staging and test.',
    'Job Separation and Employee Transfer data prep cut from <strong>1 hour</strong> to <strong>10–12 minutes</strong>.',
  ]}
  next={{ href: '/work/java-modernization/', kicker: 'Next · Case study 02', title: 'Modernizing a legacy Java UI suite →' }}
>
  <Fragment slot="context">
    <p>ePMS (performance management) and HRMS are modules of the same enterprise ERP. In ePMS, an employee's review moved from Objective Setting all the way to a 360° feedback review, with its own forms, approvals and rules at every stage.</p>
    <p>In HRMS, the basic flow covered five features end to end: creating and verifying an employee, applying a transfer and verifying it in the list, applying a job separation and verifying it in the list, a higher-study application and a travel application.</p>
    <p>Regression was manual: about two hours per run, repeated across environments.</p>
  </Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="problem">
    <p>Three things made automation hard: form data that changed from run to run, behaviour that differed between dev, staging and test, and multi-stage flows where one early failure blocked everything after it.</p>
    <p>A second problem sat outside regression. Job Separation and Employee Transfer are two of HRMS's longest flows, and checking reports, running cross-module tests or testing a related change request all needed employees already taken through them. Preparing that data by hand took an hour each time.</p>
  </Fragment>

  <div slot="figure" class="cs-figures reveal">
    <figure class="cs-figure">
      <ol class="pipeline">
        <li><span class="label">01</span>Environment config<span class="pipeline-sub">dev · staging · test</span></li>
        <li><span class="label">02</span>Fixtures<span class="pipeline-sub">pytest</span></li>
        <li><span class="label">03</span>ePMS + HRMS flows<span class="pipeline-sub">Playwright</span></li>
        <li><span class="label">04</span>Tests<span class="pipeline-sub">regression · smoke</span></li>
        <li class="is-last"><span class="label">05</span>Allure report<span class="pipeline-sub">readable by anyone</span></li>
      </ol>
      <figcaption>How the regression framework was layered, from configuration to report. Generalised; no proprietary code.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <aside class="callout" aria-labelledby="dataprep-title">
      <div class="callout-figure">
        <p class="label">Alongside the suite</p>
        <p class="callout-num">5× faster</p>
        <p class="caption">One hour of manual setup became 10–12 minutes.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="callout-body">
        <h3 id="dataprep-title">Data-prep scripts for HRMS's longest flows</h3>
        <p>Two scenario-based scripts walk Job Separation and Employee Transfer from start to finish, so employees in exactly the right state were ready in minutes instead of an hour. I used them for:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Report checks</li>
          <li>Cross-module tests</li>
          <li>Change requests on these two flows</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="caption">Kept separate from regression and smoke runs, by design: they create data; the suite checks behaviour.</p>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </div>

  <Fragment slot="looking-back">
    <p>This was my work at BRAC IT Services until October 2026; I no longer maintain it. If I built it again, I'd wire it into a CI pipeline from day one and prepare test data through APIs rather than the UI, to cut the run time further.</p>
    <p style="font-size: 16px">See the public version of this pattern: <a href="https://github.com/nawer-faria">playwright-pytest-blueprint</a> (in progress).</p>
  </Fragment>
</CaseStudy>
